tted-repairs-to-a-dam-in-2017-when-it-failed-water-and-sediment-filled-a-neighbours-pond-and-an-appeals-court-has-upheld-554294-35-in-trespass-and-nuisance-damages/articleshow/135963376.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-19T21:55:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135963558,imgsize-1751828.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Pennsylvania finds Walmart child labour violations; retailer agrees to pay $7.8m after injuries]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135956296.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Walmart has reached a settlement in response to a Pennsylvania investigation that uncovered serious breaches of child labour laws. The probe identified instances of young workers facing excessive hours and lacking work permits across various locations. As part of the settlement, Walmart will incur penalties of $7.8 million and must adopt stricter compliance protocols to safeguard young employees, setting a crucial benchmark in tackling child labour issues in the state.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/pennsylvania-investigated-walmart-after-reports-of-underage-workers-being-injured-and-found-repeated-breaches-of-child-labour-rules-the-retailer-has-agreed-to-pay-7-8-million-and-change-its-practices/articleshow/135956296.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/pennsylvania-investigated-walmart-after-reports-of-underage-workers-being-injured-and-found-repeated-breaches-of-child-labour-rules-the-retailer-has-agreed-to-pay-7-8-million-and-change-its-practices/articleshow/135956296.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-19T21:52:37+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135956639,imgsize-1498017.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Scientists found 37 carpet pythons in Cape York and recorded one growing 33.5 cm in 848 days]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135983136.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/wildlife/scientists-found-37-carpet-pythons-in-cape-york-woodlands-discovered-rodents-in-their-diet-and-recorded-one-snake-growing-33-5-cm-in-just-848-days/articleshow/135983136.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/wildlife/scientists-found-37-carpet-pythons-in-cape-york-woodlands-discovered-rodents-in-their-diet-and-recorded-one-snake-growing-33-5-cm-in-just-848-days/articleshow/135983136.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-19T21:52:32+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135983329,imgsize-173101.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['There is no private individual who has helped Ukraine more than I have': Elon Musk says Russia would have won the war if Ukraine did not have Starlink]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135998158.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/there-is-no-private-individual-who-has-helped-ukraine-more-than-i-have-elon-musk-says-russia-would-have-won-the-war-if-ukraine-did-not-have-starlink/articleshow/135998158.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/there-is-no-private-individual-who-has-helped-ukraine-more-than-i-have-elon-musk-says-russia-would-have-won-the-war-if-ukraine-did-not-have-starlink/articleshow/135998158.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-19T21:36:53+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Poulomi Ghosh</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135998382,imgsize-35292.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Unpaid Settlement Lawsuit: Newmans sue association and 33 residents; $200,000 settlement shares remain unpaid]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135977761.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[In De Pere, Wisconsin, a family faces a contentious dispute with their homeowners association regarding a fence. After winning a $200,000 settlement for being denied permission to build a fence for their children, tensions have escalated. The association has spread the financial burden among property owners, many of whom have failed to contribute.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-wisconsin-couple-who-sued-their-neighborhood-association-for-a-fence-so-their-five-children-could-play-safely-won-200000-and-now-they-are-suing-33-neighbors-who-never-paid-their-1350-share/articleshow/135977761.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-wisconsin-couple-who-sued-their-neighborhood-association-for-a-fence-so-their-five-children-could-play-safely-won-200000-and-now-they-are-suing-33-neighbors-who-never-paid-their-1350-share/articleshow/135977761.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-19T21:07:49+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135977822,imgsize-699901.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Zeynab Javadli, ex-wife of Dubai prince Sheikh Saeed, alleges UAE officials drugged her, took daughters]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135996826.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Zeynab Javadli, former wife of Dubai prince Sheikh Saeed bin Maktoum, has approached the United Nations seeking an investigation into allegations that UAE officials assaulted and drugged her during a raid in which her three daughters were taken away. Her legal team has also raised concerns over her alleged torture in custody and the children's whereabouts.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/middle-east/zeynab-javadli-ex-wife-of-dubai-prince-sheikh-saeed-bin-maktoum-alleges-uae-officials-assaulted-and-drugged-her-before-taking-away-her-three-daughters-approaches-un-seeking-investigation/articleshow/135996826.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/middle-east/zeynab-javadli-ex-wife-of-dubai-prince-sheikh-saeed-bin-maktoum-alleges-uae-officials-assaulted-and-drugged-her-before-taking-away-her-three-daughters-approaches-un-seeking-investigation/articleshow/135996826.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-19T20:53:24+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135996978,imgsize-72930.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[In 2023, teams began removing invasive spotted bass from South Africa's Breekkrans River]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135938756.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A dedicated conservation initiative along the Breekkrans River is tackling the dangers of invasive spotted bass. The project aims to safeguard the critically endangered doring fiery redfin, which is currently struggling for survival. By eradicating these invasive fish, the redfin’s habitat will expand, giving it a better chance of thriving. Innovative removal methods are employed while also creating job opportunities for the local community, thereby bolstering freshwater conservation efforts.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/nature/in-2023-teams-began-removing-invasive-spotted-bass-from-south-africas-breekkrans-river-by-2026-the-critically-endangered-doring-fiery-redfins-accessible-habitat-had-grown-from-2km-to-10km/articleshow/135938756.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/nature/in-2023-teams-began-removing-invasive-spotted-bass-from-south-africas-breekkrans-river-by-2026-the-critically-endangered-doring-fiery-redfins-accessible-habitat-had-grown-from-2km-to-10km/articleshow/135938756.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-19T21:07:44+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135938756,imgsize-407248.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Stephen Miller puts DHS Secretary Markwayne Mullin in 'primetime timeout' after Fox News interview sparks White House fury]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135996879.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/stephen-miller-puts-dhs-secretary-markwayne-mullin-in-primetime-timeout-after-fox-news-interview-sparks-white-house-fury/articleshow/135996879.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/stephen-miller-puts-dhs-secretary-markwayne-mullin-in-primetime-timeout-after-fox-news-interview-sparks-white-house-fury/articleshow/135996879.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-19T20:44:38+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Poulomi Ghosh</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135996967,imgsize-101610.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[US warns Americans in Middle East of potential attacks, flight disruptions amid rising Iran-Houthi tensions]]></title><description>&lt;img bor